From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: App Management calls Android apps Android apps

An Android app someone installed in Waydroid reaches Chrome as a NickelOS
host app, like their Linux apps, so its App Management page said "Linux
app". nickel-appd gives such an app the package id android:<package>
(nickel-appd's Waydroid source), and the page now says "Android app",
ChromeOS's own string for its Android apps.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_apps_page/app_management_page/app_details_item.ts b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_apps_page/app_management_page/app_details_item.ts
index 343476f6b762c..7449386f7f310 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_apps_page/app_management_page/app_details_item.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_apps_page/app_management_page/app_details_item.ts
@@ -343,8 +343,12 @@ export class AppManagementAppDetailsItem extends
   private getTypeAndSourceString_(app: App): string {
     if (app.type === AppType.kNickelHost) {
       // NickelOS: what installed the app, from the package id nickel-appd
-      // gives it (flatpak:..., portage, appimage:...).
+      // gives it (flatpak:..., portage, appimage:...). An Android app the
+      // user installed in Waydroid (android:<package>) is an Android app.
       const id = app.publisherId || '';
+      if (id.startsWith('android:')) {
+        return this.i18n('appManagementAppDetailsTypeAndroid');
+      }
       const installer = id.startsWith('flatpak:') ? 'Flatpak' :
           id === 'portage'                      ? 'Portage' :
           id.startsWith('appimage:')            ? 'AppImage' :
